From: qforge
Subject: [PATCH] rendervulkan: mappable images on a GPU without cached+coherent memory

A mappable image (screenshots, captures) asks findMemoryType() for a
HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT | HOST_CACHED type and hands whatever comes
back to vkAllocateMemory unchecked. turnip only exposes that combination
when the GPU is DMA-coherent; on an Adreno 610 (SM6115) the types are
DEVICE_LOCAL|HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT, DEVICE_LOCAL|HOST_VISIBLE|
HOST_CACHED and a lazily-allocated one, so the lookup returns -1 and
turnip indexes its memory-type table with 0xffffffff:

  tu_AllocateMemory (tu_device.cc:3759) <- CVulkanTexture::BInit
  (rendervulkan.cpp:2744) <- acquire_pooled_texture <-
  vulkan_acquire_screenshot_texture <- paint_all: SIGSEGV

Every screenshot request (GAMESCOPECTRL_REQUEST_SCREENSHOT, the
`screenshot` command, Steam's capture) took the whole session down.

When no cached+coherent type exists for a mappable image, fall back to
HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT, which the spec guarantees; the CPU-side
reads of a screenshot are merely slower. And if no type fits at all, fail
BInit with an error instead of passing -1 to the driver.

(qforge: HW, MANGMI Air X, 2026-10-10. Two cores: coredumpctl 12346 and
16505, symbolised against the unstripped build.)
---
diff -ruN a/src/rendervulkan.cpp b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
--- a/src/rendervulkan.cpp	2026-10-10 06:31:28
+++ b/src/rendervulkan.cpp	2026-10-10 06:31:28
@@ -2672,10 +2672,25 @@
 	VkMemoryRequirements memRequirements;
 	g_device.vk.GetImageMemoryRequirements(g_device.device(), m_vkImage, &memRequirements);
 
+	int32_t nMemoryType = g_device.findMemoryType( properties, memRequirements.memoryTypeBits );
+	if ( nMemoryType < 0 && flags.bMappable == true )
+	{
+		// No host-visible type that is both cached and coherent. turnip on a SoC whose GPU is not
+		// DMA-coherent (e.g. Adreno 610) offers cached-only and coherent-only types; take the
+		// coherent one, which the spec guarantees, and accept slower CPU reads.
+		properties = VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_VISIBLE_BIT | VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_COHERENT_BIT;
+		nMemoryType = g_device.findMemoryType( properties, memRequirements.memoryTypeBits );
+	}
+	if ( nMemoryType < 0 )
+	{
+		vk_log.errorf( "no memory type for image: properties 0x%x, type bits 0x%x", properties, memRequirements.memoryTypeBits );
+		return false;
+	}
+
 	VkMemoryAllocateInfo allocInfo = {
 		.sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_MEMORY_ALLOCATE_INFO,
 		.allocationSize = memRequirements.size,
-		.memoryTypeIndex = uint32_t(g_device.findMemoryType(properties, memRequirements.memoryTypeBits)),
+		.memoryTypeIndex = uint32_t( nMemoryType ),
 	};
 
 	m_size = allocInfo.allocationSize;
